# rm507, the empty place setting (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm507
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rm_emmerich_greyridge
written_by codex
title the empty place setting
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=servant
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk practises_laying_a_table_for_the_guest_who_never_arrives
likes mutton_stew cards tidy_house autumn_wind
dislikes drizzle haggling
fears a_chipped_cup_on_the_best_cloth cold_stew_after_a_long_shift
hopes a_supper_set_without_measuring a_quiet_evening_to_remember
topics work +0.5 family +0.3 home +0.4
styles comfort=quiet gossip=discreet refuse=plain tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# can lay a table square using a playing card for a measure and leaves one place clear of anything that might need polishing.

words
oath! = Gravy on the minutes | Soot on a clean cuff
saying! = The spoon needs no written invitation | An empty plate can wait its turn
measure = my old court card | a card with a worn red back
tablespan = the narrow edge | a card's width of cloth
spoonrest = the folded square | the crease to the right
chairgap = my unoccupied place | a clear chair space
steamskin = a thin gravy shine | the top of the stew
smudge = my travelling smoke mark | a grey cuff
stiffcloth = a well-ironed fold | the cloth's upright edge
shortwind = a brisk autumn gust | a stirring at the linen
glassmark = a tired pale ring | the faint cup circle
compass = my straight fork | a fork laid true

any
opinion @1 city for 1 : A cup can travel up three stairs and across two offices here without leaving the knowledge of anyone who has to wash it. It's home.
opinion @1 merchants against 1 : A new price written across yesterday's figure remains an increase, even in particularly good handwriting.
opinion @1 houses mixed 1 : The initials embroidered on a napkin don't explain who washed it this morning. They also don't stop it serving a guest perfectly well.
opinion @1 drink mixed 0 : A cup of something pleasant is welcome if I am free to clear my own empty cup.
opinion @1 times mixed 0 : A full bowl generally improves my view of the afternoon. I'd defer a grander judgement until after the washing up.

grown
line @1 greet : My empty setting admits another caller.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Welcome. There's no form to fill for a chair.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning light requires a fresh inspection of my cuffs.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : There's a little light left on the polished edge.
line @5 greet [self.working=yes] : Leave me the aisle that a laden plate requires.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : I've set a genuinely easy chair for family.
line @1 again.open : Another visit duly noticed and quite willingly received.
line @1 greet.return : Your greeting reached me before any formal notice.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Yours is a voice I'd make time for between courses.
line @1 farewell : Take your leave without accounting for the spoons.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll see to whatever the table has retained.
line @1 react.news : What part should go in the account before the remarks?
line @1 react.news.new : An item newly arrived on my afternoon docket.
line @1 react.news.known : An existing matter in a handsomer hand.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Was anybody present who could sign for that assertion?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Empty chairs should be allowed to mean different things to each household.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That deserves a better cup than the ordinary one.
line @1 answer.how : Adequate to the work. The clean plates have offered no objection.
line @1 ask.how : What part of your day would you mark complete?
line @1 sympathise : I'd reserve your chair if that would ease the evening.
line @1 reassure : A bowl and a chair require very little explanation.
line @1 decline : I've still a formal engagement with the plates already standing beside me.
line @1 accept_decline : My small request has been put away with its proper papers.
line @1 preclose : I've one unused setting to lift before the cloth comes off.
line @1 ack : Entered.
scene setting
when topic=work self.job=servant self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've worn a playing card smooth measuring the space between a plate and the edge.
b : Why that distance? | Is counting really necessary?
a : Far enough inside to spare a sleeve, near enough to reach without pulling the dish forward. | No. But I've yet to find a guest who objected to the result of the experiment.

scene card
when topic=pastimes self.likes=cards
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I play with a clean deck. The single card I measure by would give the whole game away.
b : How could you recognise it? | Why keep a card for measuring?
a : One corner has acquired the shine of an extensively handled spoon. | It's flat, it's ready, and it has never yet asked for a reference.

scene stew
when topic=food self.likes=mutton_stew
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In a sound bowl the gravy finds a proper level before the tray leaves my palms.
b : Is thick gravy better? | Do you examine your own supper that way?
a : For a journey upstairs it certainly travels with greater decorum. | My own supper generally enters a shorter and more direct procedure.

scene order
when topic=home self.likes=tidy_house
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : To my mind a tidy room still has one place where a guest may put something down.
b : Doesn't a spare place invite clutter? | What belongs in your own spare space?
a : It invites an actual use. I see a small distinction worth preserving. | A letter awaiting an answer, provided the answer wasn't to be put off for a fortnight.

scene wind
when topic=season self.likes=autumn_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A gust through an autumn window will find the one napkin I have yet to fold.
b : Do you chase it? | Would you close the window?
a : I wait where the table slopes slightly. Most napkins have a poor understanding of escape. | After giving the place some fresh air. The gust's performed a service and needn't stay for dinner.

scene haggling
when topic=prices self.dislikes=haggling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a price with enough confidence in itself to remain on the label.
b : Would you ask for less? | Can a label be wrong?
a : I'd buy a lesser article if I could afford no better. I dislike the business of coaxing numbers about. | Certainly. That's why I read it before I part with anything.

scene drip
when topic=weather self.dislikes=drizzle
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A drizzle will add a grey margin to clean cuffs while the sky claims it's doing nothing.
b : Would you change your cuffs? | What keeps a spattered cuff useful?
a : If there's an important plate to carry. An ordinary errand may have my ordinary sleeves. | Turn it in briefly, then wash it as soon as work permits. It doesn't merit a written defence.

scene smoke
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I find a faint smoky scent follows my coat quite independently of its laundry arrangements.
b : Does it trouble the guests? | Have you tried airing it?
a : I keep it well clear of the food. A smell in a coat is less intrusive on a hook. | The result was a very well aired smell of smoke.

scene spouse
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd gladly set an uncomplicated supper for #self.spouse#.
b : Would you measure that setting too? | What counts as uncomplicated?
a : Habit might lead my fingers to the card. I'll exercise restraint and occupy the spare chair myself. | One pot, two bowls, and a table whose arrangement can be understood without a clerk.

scene office
when topic=home self.quarter=office
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In the Office quarter a leaf caught in the passage can look surprisingly like a lost petition.
b : Would you pick it up? | How can a leaf resemble paper?
a : I do. A leaf is an easy matter to conclude, and a petition may be somebody's whole morning. | Flat, pale and generally moving in whatever direction the clerk would least prefer.

scene learn
when topic=work self.apprentice=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I practise with an empty plate before I attempt a difficult turn carrying a full one.
b : What's there to learn with no weight? | Do you report a dropped plate?
a : Where my elbow will go when somebody moves a chair. The gravy can join the experiment later. | Yes, with the pieces accounted for. A missing chip can cause a guest more difficulty than a missing plate.

scene loss
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A spare chair at supper carries enough of its own meaning without a public inscription.
b : Would you have somebody sit there? | Is it always set out?
a : Good company is welcome to choose. I don't require an explanation from a guest or an empty seat. | Some evenings. I allow the household a little liberty about its private arrangements.

scene coins
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A bargain spoon with a crack at the neck is a modest charge for an awkward supper.
b : Would you return it? | Can a crack be seen?
a : With its price token if I had one. The seller and I should be able to discuss the actual article. | Lay it in full light, then tilt the handle. I also notice when the handle flexes.

scene boss
when topic=work self.job=servant self.boss
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An instruction from #self.boss# is easier to carry out when I repeat the number of settings before leaving.
b : Does that sound formal? | What if a guest is late?
a : Briefly. Considerably less formal than explaining a whole tray of additional dishes. | I set a place and keep the food warm separately. The guest can arrive without encountering a chilled welcome.

scene dark
when topic=day here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In weak light I know my measuring card by the clipped corner.
b : Have you ever laid it out with dinner? | Which corner is clipped?
a : Once it came very near a bread plate. Happily no guest had ordered a hand of cards. | The corner my thumb reaches first. A servant's apparatus can be simple if it's consistent.

scene sleep
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : After a day carrying dishes I like to set my arms flat along a table for a minute.
b : Does that ease the shoulders? | Won't the table need polishing?
a : It gives them a moment without a matter to convey. That's a measurable improvement. | My personal table has kindly excused itself from formal inspection.

scene facts
when topic=news
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd split a dinner account into what was ordered and what actually reached the table.
b : Where do you put a rumour? | Would you put a guest's complaint on it?
a : Below the line, in pencil. A kitchen deserves its facts in a more durable hand. | If I heard it myself. Complaints improve very little in transit.

story whitelinen [topic=work self.job=servant]
  : I laid a white cloth to a measured border and found one corner apparently an inch too long.
  : The opposite chair had caught the hem under one wooden arm. The cloth was perfectly blameless.
  b : Did you correct the chair?
  : I released the hem without entering a complaint against the furniture.

story cardstew [topic=food]
  : A small drop of gravy landed in the centre of my measuring card just below the queen's chin.
  : I wiped it promptly and left a shadow like a small official collar about that distinguished neck.
  b : Does the collar remain?
  : It does. I've promoted the card to measuring napkins and entrusted the spoons to another court.

story windowleaf [topic=season]
  : An autumn leaf blew through a high window and came to rest on a vacant dinner plate.
  : I carried it outside with the same care I'd ordinarily grant the intended dish.
  b : Was there a reason for the ceremony?
  : I didn't want wet leaf juice on the cloth. One can arrive at excellent manners by thoroughly practical means.

rule @tray
when concept=bark self.job=servant self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Clear hand under the broadest plate. | Leave a card's width at the near edge.

rule @card
when concept=bark self.likes=cards
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The clipped queen's on measuring duty. | A sound deck if we're actually playing.

rule @drizzle
when concept=bark self.dislikes=drizzle
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Change that cuff before the next course. | The little wet spots do count.

rule @dusk
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep a lamp by the folded border. | Last of the light on clean silver.

dlg @1 resident.hub : The spare setting can be moved quite easily. Sit here.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : Your place won't require a fresh introduction, #topic.player#.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : State the purpose plainly and let the table keep its distance.
dlg @4 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Enough lamplight for a civil word and one unchipped cup.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=servant] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. Dishes, messages and the occasional extraordinary request pass through my hands.
dlg @2 resident.job : I try to send the guest away remembering supper and forgetting how much work it took.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : Here's an item I can enter in plain handwriting. #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Leave your cup on the table. I'll take it with the rest.
graft @clippedqueen resident.hub
choice Why is a playing card lying by the fork? -> clippedqueen
node clippedqueen
say The clipped queen gives me a convenient width to measure by. Without drawing a mark I can give each setting an equal share of the edge.
choice Does the queen come to dinner? -> clippedqueen_more
choice Look over the table. -> hub
node clippedqueen_more
say Only to the preparation. I retire the card before the first dish arrives. The queen has never raised a formal objection.
choice Look over the table. -> hub
choice Leave the measurements alone. -> bye
